# Valkey default config and init scripts contain comments and variables mentioning "password" keywords — false positive.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0109 (ConfigMap with secrets)
KSV-0109
AVD-KSV-0109

# Valkey init scripts and Lighttpd CORS header configuration (Access-Control-Allow-Headers containing Authorization) — false positive.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-01010 (ConfigMap with sensitive content)
KSV-01010
AVD-KSV-01010

# Synapse dynamically generates secrets.yaml into /synapse/config/conf.d at startup; Hookshot, Lighttpd, and Mautrix bridges write runtime/cache data to root filesystem. Upstream test pods also do not set readOnlyRootFilesystem.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0014 (Root file system is not read-only)
KSV-0014
AVD-KSV-0014

# Upstream Helm test hook pods (matrix-synapse-test-connection, valkey-test-auth-existing) use default unhardened security contexts (helm test only, never run in production).
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0118 (Default security context configured)
KSV-0118
AVD-KSV-0118

# Synapse volume-permissions init container and Hookshot upstream container run as root; Lighttpd starts as root to configure and drop privileges to user lighttpd. Upstream test pods run as root.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0012 (Runs as root user)
KSV-0012
AVD-KSV-0012

# Upstream Synapse volume-permissions init container and Helm test hook pods do not configure allowPrivilegeEscalation: false.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0001 (Can elevate its own privileges)
KSV-0001
AVD-KSV-0001

# Upstream matrix-synapse chart test hook (matrix-synapse-test-connection) uses hardcoded busybox image without explicit tag or digest.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0013 (Image tag ':latest' used)
KSV-0013
AVD-KSV-0013

# Upstream Helm test hook pods (test-connection, test-auth-existing) do not configure RuntimeDefault seccomp profile.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0104 (Seccomp policies disabled)
KSV-0104
AVD-KSV-0104

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0030 (Runtime/Default Seccomp profile not set)
KSV-0030
AVD-KSV-0030

# Lighttpd requires default capabilities to drop privileges to user lighttpd; upstream Helm test hook pods do not drop capabilities.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0003 (Default capabilities: some containers do not drop all)
KSV-0003
AVD-KSV-0003

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0004 (Default capabilities: some containers do not drop any)
KSV-0004
AVD-KSV-0004

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0106 (Container capabilities must only include NET_BIND_SERVICE)
KSV-0106
AVD-KSV-0106

# Upstream subchart Helm test hook pods (test-connection, test-auth-existing) do not specify CPU resource requests.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0015 (CPU requests not specified)
KSV-0015
AVD-KSV-0015

# Upstream subchart Helm test hook pods (test-connection, test-auth-existing) do not specify memory resource requests.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0016 (Memory requests not specified)
KSV-0016
AVD-KSV-0016

# Upstream matrix-synapse chart volume-permissions init container explicitly sets runAsUser: 0 to chown /synapse/data volume permissions.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0105 (Containers must not set runAsUser to 0)
KSV-0105
